<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka says no damage in Wednesday oil attack.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka says no damage in Wednesday oil attack.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tamil Tiger rebels attacked a state oil depot in Sri Lanka's eastern Batticaloa district early on Wednesday but there was no damage to oil tanks, military officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Six policemen guarding the oil depot owned by the state-run Ceylon Petroleum Corporation were wounded in the attack by Liberation Tigers of Tamil Eelam (LTTE) rebels, they said.</p>
<p>No other details were given.</p>
<p>The LTTE rebels are fighting for an independent homeland for minority Tamils in predominantly Sinhalese Sri Lanka.</p>
</text>
